{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"storeURI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device-local by design: it must never be synced, exported, or adopted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from another device’s data. Object URIs carry a store UUID and primary"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"key, so a foreign URI is meaningless here at best — and on a device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restored from another device’s backup (matching store UUID) it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolve to the wrong object. Entries are disposable: a missing or stale"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URI is re-populated wherever the object surfaces next — attach import,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"save capture, or integration creating the object for an insert change.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(An update or delete change whose identifier has no usable URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped for that pass, not re-resolved.)","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/globalidentifier\/storeuri"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The local object’s "},{"code":"NSManagedObjectID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URI — the essential mapping from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this global identifier to its row in THIS device’s persistent store,"},